module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.Sheaf
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Stalk
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.MaximalIdeal.Defs

/-!
# Stalks of module sheaves on a scheme

For a scheme `X` and an `𝒪_X`-module `M : X.Modules`, the stalk of the underlying abelian
presheaf `M.presheaf` at a point `x` is a module over the stalk `𝒪_{X,x}`. Mathlib constructs
that module structure, under a long autogenerated name spelled out in the body of
`Stacks.ModuleStalk.stalkModule` below, but instance search does not find it through the
`Scheme.Modules` wrapper. So this file names it and develops the API that statements about
germs of sections need:

* germs are `𝒪_{X,x}`-semilinear in the obvious sense (`Stacks.ModuleStalk.germ_smul`);
* a morphism of `𝒪_X`-modules induces an `𝒪_{X,x}`-linear map of stalks
  (`Stacks.ModuleStalk.map`), and an isomorphism induces a linear equivalence
  (`Stacks.ModuleStalk.equivOfIso`);
* the submodule `𝔪_x · M_x` of the stalk (`Stacks.ModuleStalk.maximalSmul`) is carried onto
  `𝔪_x · N_x` by the stalk equivalence of an isomorphism `M ≅ N`
  (`Stacks.ModuleStalk.maximalSmul_map`).

The last item is what makes the vanishing condition "`s ∉ 𝔪_x M_x`" of Stacks Tag 01CY, and hence
ampleness, transport along isomorphisms of modules; see
`Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus_congr`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ModuleStalk.stalkModule`: the `𝒪_{X,x}`-module structure on `M_x`, a `scoped instance`.
* `Stacks.ModuleStalk.mapFun`, `Stacks.ModuleStalk.map`: the map of stalks induced by a morphism
  of `𝒪_X`-modules, as a bare function and as an `𝒪_{X,x}`-linear map.
* `Stacks.ModuleStalk.equivOfIso`: the linear equivalence of stalks induced by an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.ModuleStalk.maximalSmul`: the submodule `𝔪_x · M_x` of the stalk at `x`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ModuleStalk.germ_smul`, `Stacks.ModuleStalk.Γgerm_smul`: germs respect scalars.
* `Stacks.ModuleStalk.mapFun_germ`: the stalk map sends the germ of `t` to the germ of `φ t`.
* `Stacks.ModuleStalk.maximalSmul_map`: `𝔪_x · M_x` maps onto `𝔪_x · N_x` along an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.ModuleStalk.mem_maximalSmul_mapFun_iff`: membership in `𝔪_x · N_x` of the image of a
  stalk element under an isomorphism is membership of the element in `𝔪_x · M_x`.
* `Stacks.ModuleStalk.smul_mem_maximalSmul_iff`: `r • m ∈ 𝔪_x · M_x` precisely when `r` is a
  non-unit or `m ∈ 𝔪_x · M_x`. This is the arithmetic behind the Stacks remark
  `X_s ∩ X_{s'} = X_{ss'}` in the case where `s'` is a section of the structure sheaf.

## Design choice

The module structure is a `scoped instance` rather than a global one. Two other files in this
repository already name stalk-module instances for differently-wrapped base sheaves
(`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/LocallyFreeRank.lean`, Stacks Tag 01C9), and a
global instance for the `Scheme.Modules` wrapper would be a cross-cutting change to instance
search for every consumer of `X.Modules`. Opening
`Stacks.ModuleStalk` is enough, and no consumer of the *definitions* below needs the instance:
the elaborated terms carry it.

## Implementation notes

**Transparency gotcha 1: the instance is not found.** `X.Modules` is
`SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf` and `X.ringCatSheaf.obj` is `X.presheaf ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat
RingCat` only after unfolding `sheafCompose`. Mathlib's stalk-module instance is stated for a
`PresheafOfModules (R ⋙ forget₂ _ _)` with `R : X.Presheaf CommRingCat`, and instance search
will not unfold the wrapper to match. The instance below supplies it with `R := X.presheaf`
written out. Unlike the Tag 01C9 instances named above, no transparency option is needed for
this: the application elaborates at default transparency.

**Transparency gotcha 2: `stalk` versus `stalkFunctor.obj`.** `TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F x` is by
definition `(TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor C x).obj F`, but the two spellings are not
interchangeable for instance search, which looks at the syntactic head. Applying
`(stalkFunctor Ab x).map φ.mapPresheaf` directly inside a goal produces a term whose type is
spelled `(stalkFunctor Ab x).obj N.presheaf`, and `HSMul` then fails to synthesise. The
definition `mapFun` exists only to force the `stalk` spelling once and for all; every lemma
below is stated about `mapFun`, never about the raw functor application.

**Why germs, not functoriality, prove the composition laws.** `mapFun_comp` and `mapFun_id`
could be derived from functoriality of `stalkFunctor ∘ toPresheaf`, but doing so leaves goals
mentioning `Scheme.Modules.Hom.mapPresheaf` of a composite, where the rewrite has to happen
underneath a `ConcreteCategory.hom` coercion. Reducing to germs first
(`TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq`) keeps every goal in the `germ` spelling, where
`mapFun_germ` applies on the nose.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CY)

## What is not done

The stalk `M_x` is never identified with anything concrete: in particular the stalk of the
structure sheaf *as an abelian group* is not identified with `𝒪_{X,x}` *as a ring*, so nothing
here computes `𝔪_x · M_x` for `M` the structure sheaf. Nothing here proves that the locus where
a germ avoids `𝔪_x M_x` is open — that is Stacks Tag 01CY, which needs local freeness of `M`;
it is proved, as `Stacks.NonvanishingOpen.isOpen_nonvanishingLocus`
(`../NonvanishingOpen/Basic.lean`), from a sectionwise trivialization rather than from anything
in this file. No finiteness, coherence or quasi-coherence hypothesis appears here, and
Nakayama's lemma is not used.
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.ModuleStalk

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} {M N K : X.Modules}

/-- The `𝒪_{X,x}`-module structure on the stalk of an `𝒪_X`-module at `x`. This is Mathlib's
stalk-module instance for presheaves of modules over a sheaf of commutative rings, applied with
the base presheaf written as `X.presheaf`; see the implementation notes for why instance search
does not find it through the `Scheme.Modules` wrapper. -/
noncomputable scoped instance stalkModule (M : X.Modules) (x : X) :
    Module (X.presheaf.stalk x) (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) :=
  PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
    (R := X.presheaf) M.val x

/-- The germ of a scalar multiple of a section is the scalar multiple of the germs. -/
theorem germ_smul (M : X.Modules) (x : X) (U : X.Opens) (hx : x ∈ U)
    (a : Γ(X, U)) (t : Γ(M, U)) :
    (M.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom (a • t) =
      (X.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom a • (M.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom t :=
  PresheafOfModules.germ_smul (R := X.presheaf) M.val x U hx a t

/-- `germ_smul` for global sections. -/
theorem Γgerm_smul (M : X.Modules) (x : X) (a : Γ(X, ⊤)) (t : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    (M.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (a • t) =
      (X.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom a • (M.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom t :=
  germ_smul M x ⊤ True.intro a t

/-- The map of stalks induced by a morphism of `𝒪_X`-modules, as a bare function. The point of
this definition is that its type is spelled with `TopCat.Presheaf.stalk`; see the implementation
notes. -/
noncomputable def mapFun (φ : M ⟶ N) (x : X) :
    TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x →
      TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) N.presheaf x :=
  fun m => ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor Ab.{u} x).map φ.mapPresheaf).hom m

/-- The stalk map sends the germ of a section `t` to the germ of its image. -/
theorem mapFun_germ (φ : M ⟶ N) (x : X) (U : X.Opens) (hx : x ∈ U) (t : Γ(M, U)) :
    mapFun φ x ((M.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom t) =
      (N.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom (φ.app U t) :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply U x hx φ.mapPresheaf t

/-- `mapFun_germ` for global sections. -/
theorem mapFun_Γgerm (φ : M ⟶ N) (x : X) (t : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    mapFun φ x ((M.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom t) = (N.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (φ.app ⊤ t) :=
  mapFun_germ φ x ⊤ True.intro t

/-- The stalk map `mapFun φ x` is additive. -/
theorem mapFun_add (φ : M ⟶ N) (x : X)
    (m m' : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) :
    mapFun φ x (m + m') = mapFun φ x m + mapFun φ x m' :=
  map_add _ m m'

/-- The stalk map of a morphism of `𝒪_X`-modules is `𝒪_{X,x}`-linear. -/
theorem mapFun_smul (φ : M ⟶ N) (x : X) (r : X.presheaf.stalk x)
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) :
    mapFun φ x (r • m) = r • mapFun φ x m := by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, t, ht⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq M.presheaf m
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, a, ha⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq X.presheaf r
  have hxU : x ∈ V ⊓ W := ⟨hxV, hxW⟩
  rw [← ht, ← ha, ← TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply M.presheaf
      (homOfLE (inf_le_left : V ⊓ W ≤ V)) x hxU,
    ← TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply X.presheaf (homOfLE (inf_le_right : V ⊓ W ≤ W)) x hxU,
    ← germ_smul, mapFun_germ, mapFun_germ, Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul, germ_smul]

/-- The stalk map of a composite is the composite of the stalk maps. -/
theorem mapFun_comp (φ : M ⟶ N) (ψ : N ⟶ K) (x : X)
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) :
    mapFun (φ ≫ ψ) x m = mapFun ψ x (mapFun φ x m) := by
  obtain ⟨U, hx, t, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq M.presheaf m
  rw [mapFun_germ, mapFun_germ, mapFun_germ, Scheme.Modules.Hom.comp_app]
  rfl

/-- The stalk map of the identity morphism is the identity. -/
theorem mapFun_id (M : X.Modules) (x : X)
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) : mapFun (𝟙 M) x m = m := by
  obtain ⟨U, hx, t, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq M.presheaf m
  rw [mapFun_germ, Scheme.Modules.Hom.id_app]
  rfl

/-- The `𝒪_{X,x}`-linear map of stalks induced by a morphism of `𝒪_X`-modules. -/
noncomputable def map (φ : M ⟶ N) (x : X) :
    TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x →ₗ[X.presheaf.stalk x]
      TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) N.presheaf x where
  toFun := mapFun φ x
  map_add' := mapFun_add φ x
  map_smul' := mapFun_smul φ x

/-- The linear stalk map `map φ x` acts as `mapFun φ x`. -/
@[simp] theorem map_apply (φ : M ⟶ N) (x : X)
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) : map φ x m = mapFun φ x m := rfl

/-- The `𝒪_{X,x}`-linear equivalence of stalks induced by an isomorphism of `𝒪_X`-modules. -/
noncomputable def equivOfIso (e : M ≅ N) (x : X) :
    TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x ≃ₗ[X.presheaf.stalk x]
      TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) N.presheaf x where
  toFun := mapFun e.hom x
  map_add' := mapFun_add e.hom x
  map_smul' := mapFun_smul e.hom x
  invFun := mapFun e.inv x
  left_inv m := by rw [← mapFun_comp, e.hom_inv_id, mapFun_id]
  right_inv m := by rw [← mapFun_comp, e.inv_hom_id, mapFun_id]

/-- The stalk equivalence `equivOfIso e x` acts as the stalk map of `e.hom`. -/
@[simp] theorem equivOfIso_apply (e : M ≅ N) (x : X)
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) :
    equivOfIso e x m = mapFun e.hom x m := rfl

/-- The submodule `𝔪_x · M_x` of the stalk of `M` at `x`: the scalar multiples, by the maximal
ideal of the local ring `𝒪_{X,x}`, of arbitrary stalk elements. A section of `M` is said not to
vanish at `x` when its germ avoids this submodule. -/
noncomputable def maximalSmul (M : X.Modules) (x : X) :
    Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) :=
  IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) • ⊤

/-- If `r` lies in the maximal ideal `𝔪_x` of `𝒪_{X,x}`, then `r • m` lies in `𝔪_x · M_x` for
every `m` in the stalk `M_x`. -/
theorem smul_mem_maximalSmul_of_mem_maximalIdeal {x : X} {r : X.presheaf.stalk x}
    (hr : r ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) : r • m ∈ maximalSmul M x :=
  Submodule.smul_mem_smul hr Submodule.mem_top

/-- `r • m` lies in `𝔪_x · M_x` precisely when `r` is a non-unit or `m` already lies there.
This is the arithmetic content of the Stacks remark `X_s ∩ X_{s'} = X_{ss'}`, in the case where
`s'` is a section of the structure sheaf. -/
theorem smul_mem_maximalSmul_iff {x : X} (r : X.presheaf.stalk x)
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) :
    r • m ∈ maximalSmul M x ↔ ¬ IsUnit r ∨ m ∈ maximalSmul M x := by
  refine ⟨fun h => (em' (IsUnit r)).imp_right fun hr => ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := hr
    have : (↑v⁻¹ : X.presheaf.stalk x) • ((v : X.presheaf.stalk x) • m) ∈ maximalSmul M x :=
      Submodule.smul_mem _ _ h
    rwa [smul_smul, ← Units.val_mul, inv_mul_cancel, Units.val_one, one_smul] at this
  · rintro (hr | hm)
    · exact smul_mem_maximalSmul_of_mem_maximalIdeal
        ((IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal r).mpr hr) m
    · exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hm

/-- The submodule `𝔪_x · M_x` is carried onto `𝔪_x · N_x` by the stalk equivalence of an
isomorphism `M ≅ N`. -/
theorem maximalSmul_map (e : M ≅ N) (x : X) :
    Submodule.map (equivOfIso e x : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x →ₗ[_] _)
      (maximalSmul M x) = maximalSmul N x := by
  rw [maximalSmul, maximalSmul, Submodule.map_smul'', Submodule.map_top,
    LinearMap.range_eq_top.mpr (equivOfIso e x).surjective]

/-- Membership of `mapFun e.hom x m` in `𝔪_x · N_x` is membership of `m` in `𝔪_x · M_x`. -/
theorem mem_maximalSmul_mapFun_iff (e : M ≅ N) (x : X)
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf x) :
    mapFun e.hom x m ∈ maximalSmul N x ↔ m ∈ maximalSmul M x := by
  rw [← maximalSmul_map e x, Submodule.mem_map_equiv]
  exact Iff.of_eq (congrArg (· ∈ maximalSmul M x) ((equivOfIso e x).symm_apply_apply m))

end Stacks.ModuleStalk

end
